Sources for `plan-review` skill (see plans/skill-audits/plan-review.md for full audit):

- gstack /plan-ceo-review (1434 LOC + sections) — the CEO lens: premise/leverage/trajectory challenge, mandatory weighted alternatives, and the four scope modes (EXPANSION/SELECTIVE/HOLD/REDUCTION). The EXPANSION mode is the plan-level "10x" move.
- gstack /plan-eng-review (990 LOC + sections) — the Eng lens: architecture soundness, four-data-path failure modes, the deep test-coverage trace + regression-iron-rule + coverage map, performance.
- gstack /plan-design-review (1455 LOC + sections) — the Design lens: IA hierarchy, interaction-state coverage, journey/emotional arc, AI-slop classifier, responsive/a11y.
- gstack /plan-devex-review (1418 LOC + sections) — the DevEx lens: developer journey, time-to-first-value (TTHW) vs competitors, error-message quality, docs, upgrade path.
- gstack /autoplan (1810 LOC) — distilled into the `all` MODE (not a separate skill): fixed CEO→Design→Eng→DX order, the decision taxonomy (Mechanical auto / Taste + User-challenge escalate), the 6 decision principles, cross-lens theme synthesis, single final gate.
- OpenAI "designing delightful frontends" + Steve Krug "Don't Make Me Think" — re-cited for the Design lens' slop bar and usability laws (paraphrased, not pasted).

Strategy: distill (5 sources → 1 skill, 129 LOC). Chosen over 4-5 dedicated skills (anti-bloat: one subject = "critique a written plan"; mirrors code-review's one-skill-many-dimensions) and over extending writing-plans (authoring != adversarial multi-persona critique; would overlap >30%). autoplan dissolves into a mode (YAGNI). See docs/DECISIONS.md (2026-07-10, DEV-385).

Rejected (not vendored): all gstack runtime (preamble bash, gbrain, telemetry, plan-mode detection, AskUserQuestion D-numbering/completeness machinery, Codex-CLI invocation, voice/writing-style); the named-founder "Cognitive Patterns — How Great X Think" rosters (highest copy-risk, least load-bearing — the value is the checks, not the name-dropping); the dx-hall-of-fame.md exemplar corpus (calibration reference, not methodology). The shared substrate (scope gate, one-finding-one-question, registries, task list, verdict, second-opinion) was factored ONCE rather than duplicated per lens to stay under the 30% cross-lens overlap cap.
